\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_OBJECT_NEXT}}}{\b\fs20\ul Next Object Placement Settings:
\par 
\par }{\fs20 This tool is used to create a sense of randomness and variety to groups of objects.  For example, when placing trees for a forest, this tool can randomly change the orientation and size of the trees as they are placed.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Random Orientation:
\par }{\fs20 The three checkboxes here will randomly change the axis orientation of each subsequently placed object.  The settings can be randomly changed for the X, Y, and Z-axis individually or in any combination.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Scale:
\par }{\fs20 By enabling this selection, each subsequent item placed will be randomly resized within the range defined by the minimum and maximum multipliers.  The multipliers can be set by
 the user and are calculated with the "normal" size of an object being 1.  For example, with a minimum setting of .5 and a maximum setting of 1.5, each subsequent object will be randomly sized, with the possibility of being as small as half its normal siz
e or as large as one and a half times larger than normal.  The default settings are .85 minimum and 1.5 maximum.  
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Related Editor Dialogue Windows:
\par }{\fs20 Node ~> Node Properties
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Related Siege University Courses:
\par }{\fs20 102: Objects
