\b\fs20\ul Starting Groups;
\par 
\par }{\fs20 Starting groups are clusters of starting points that indicate points on a map where players can begin a multiplayer game.  These starting points are listed in the staging area of the multiplayer games, and enable players to select 
their starting location.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Select Group:
\par }{\fs20 This is a list of all of the starting groups on the map.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul New:
\par }{\fs20 Clicking on this button will add a new entry to the "Selected Group" list and will open another dialogue window prompting the user to enter a name and description for the new starting group.
\par }{\i\fs20\ul 
\par Edit:
\par }{\fs20 Selecting a starting group from the "Selected Group" list and clicking on this button will open the Starting Group Properties dialogue window with the current properties displayed for the selected starting group.}{\i\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par Delete:
\par }{\fs20 Selecting a starting group from the "Selected Group" list and clicking on this button will delete the starting group.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Related Editor Dialogue Windows:
\par }{\fs20 View ~> Preferences
\par Objects ~> Object Properties
\par Settings ~> Starting Groups ~> Starting Group Properties
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Related Siege University Courses:
\par }{\fs20 102: Objects
\par 200: Dungeon Siege Concepts and Terminology
\par }{\f1\fs20 \page }{\cs19\f1\fs20\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_STARTING_GROUP_PROPERTIES}}}{
\b\fs20\ul Starting Group Properties:
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Group Name:
\par }{\fs20 This is the name of the starting group.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Default Group:
\par }{\fs20 Enabling this option will set the selected starting group as the default starting group.  Any new starting points added will default to that group.}{\i\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par Development-Only Group
\par }{\fs20 Enabling this option will prevent the starting group 
from showing up as an option in games played using the RETAIL version of the DungeonSiege.exe.  Only games played with the RELEASE version of the .exe will have the option to select Dev-Only starting groups in the staging area.}{\i\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par Description:
\par }{\fs20 Any information entered here will show up at the bottom of the screen in the description text box that appears in the staging area when users attempt to select their starting point.}{\i\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par Screen Name:
\par }{\fs20 The name of the starting group as it appears in the drop down list in the staging area.
\par }{\i\fs20\ul 
\par Multiplayer Levels:
\par }{\fs20 This window displays level requirements for using the selected starting group. If no level requirement is set, any character can use the starting g
roup. In the instance of additional world levels (such as the Veteran and Elite worlds in Dungeon Siege's multiplayer world), the additional world levels associated with this starting group and their corresponding level requirements are also indicated her
e.
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs20 Add Level ~
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\i\fs20 \tab }{\fs20 
Clicking this button will create a new entry in the Multiplayer Levels window and will open another dialogue window prompting the user to enter which world level requirements are being set for, and what the required character level is to u
se the starting group in the indicated world level.
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs20 Remove Level ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 Selecting a level requirement listed in the Multiplayer Levels window and clicking this button will delete the selected level requirement.
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs20 Remove all ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 Clicking on this button will remove all entries in the Multiplayer Levels window for the selected starting group
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\i\fs20\ul Related Editor Dialogue Windows:
