\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_QUEST_EDITOR}}}{\b\fs20\ul Quest Editor:
\par 
\par }{\fs20 This dialogue window is used to set quest content.  The user can use this tool to assign text descriptions, journal entries, order of steps, and other information to a quest.  Triggers control the actual }{\i\fs20 functioning}{\fs20  of a quest.}{
\b\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Settings:
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\widctlpar\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 \tab }{\i\fs20 Screen Name ~
\par }{\fs20 \tab This is the name of the quest, as it will be listed in the journal.
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs20 Quest Image ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This data field allows the user to indicate which graphic will be used as the quest image. The quest image is the small image that displays at the top of the journal page when the particular quest is highlighted in the list.
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs20 Victory Sample ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This drop down list allows the user to select which sound will play when the quest is completed.
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs20 Award Skrit ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 Using the drop down list, the user can select a skrit to be used to give a reward to the player completing the quest. 
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20 \tab Chapter ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 
As the game story develops and new chapters come into play, the journal entries are categorized according to chapter.  The drop down list here allows the user to select from a list of existing chapters to indicate in which chapter the quest is located, so
 that it can be sorted accordingly.}{\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Quest Updates:
\par }{\fs20 \tab This window shows the steps of the quest.  After each step is completed, the next step is displayed in the journal
 with updated text.  By selecting an update from the list and clicking on the "Edit" button, the user is taken to the Quest Update dialogue window, where the content of the update can be edited.
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\i\fs20\ul Related Editor Dialogue Windows:
