\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_QUEST_UPDATE}}}{\b\fs20\ul Quest Update:
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Order:
\par }{\fs20 By assigning a numeric value to this field, the user defines the order of the steps that make up the quest.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Is this a required update?
\par }{\fs20 If this box is checked, the selected step must be completed to successfully complete the quest.  Triggers to complete a quest cannot be used until all required steps are completed.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Description:
\par }{\fs20 This is the text that appears in the text box next to the quest graphic in the journal.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Speaker:
\par }{\fs20 The name entered in this field will appear above the text of the quest when the selected quest's dialogue is selected for viewing in the journal.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Conversation Address:
\par }{\fs20 In the journal, when a quest is selected and the request is made to review the dialogue, the conversation giving the quest is displayed in the journal and is accompanied by the associated sound sample, if one exists.  By using the drop down list
 here, the user defines which conversation that is by selecting the appropriate fuel file.  In this way, changes that are made to the conversation or sound sample will not require further editing of the quest.  NOTE ~ to appear in the as part of the quest
, the \'93Quest Dialogue\'94 button in the Conversation Line Editor must be checked for the indicated line of conversation.  
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\i\fs20\ul Related Editor Dialogue Windows:
