\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_CONVERSATION_LIST_GLOBAL}}}{\b\fs20\ul Map Conversation Manager:
\par }{\b\fs20 
\par }{\fs20 Similar to the "Object Conversation Manager", the Global Conversation Manager differs in that instead of listing conversations assigned to the selected object, it, instead, lists all of the conversations available within the current region.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Conversations Window:
\par }{\fs20 This is a list of all the conversations assigned to objects in the region.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul New:
\par }{\fs20 This button will open another dialogue window that will prompt the user to enter a name for the new conversation.  The new name will appear in the "Conversations" window. At th
at time, the new conversation can be edited by using the "Edit" button, which will take the user to the "Conversation Editor" dialogue window.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Edit:
\par }{\fs20 Selecting a conversation from the "Conversations" window and then clicking on this button will open the "Conversation Editor" dialogue window, where the user can edit the selected conversation.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Remove:
\par }{\fs20 Selecting a conversation from the "Conversations" window and then clicking on this button will remove the conversation from the "Conversations" window for the region.
