\b\fs20\ul Region Conversation Manager:
\par 
\par }{\fs20 This tool is used to edit or add new conversations associated with objects (actors).  In order to use the Object Conversation Manager, you must first select an actor that has a conversation block in its template.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Game Object Details:
\par }{\fs20 This area displays the screen name, template name, and SCID of the object to which the conversation is being assigned.  
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Existing Conversations:
\par }{\fs20 This window displays all conversations currently assigned to the selected actor.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul New:}{\fs20 
\par Clicking on the "New" button will open the New Conversation dialogue window, where the user can enter a name for the new conversation or select an existing conversation from the drop down menu.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Edit:
\par }{\fs20 By selecting a conversation in the Exisiting Conversations window and clicking on the "Edit" button, the Conversation Editor dialogue window will open, where the user can edit the conversation and/or edit the goodbye.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Remove:
\par }{\fs20 Selecting a conversation from the list and clicking on "Remove" will remove the conversation from the actor's list.}{\i\fs20 
