\par }{\f1\fs20 \page }{\cs19\f1\fs20\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_PATH_REPORTER}}}{\b\fs20\ul 
Tuning Path Reports:
\par 
\par }{\fs20 
This dialogue window allows the user to select which reports will be generated from the tuning path information.  Each of the reports can be generated Cumulatively or in a Per Point basis.  Cumulative reports will show the sum of all information along the
 entire tuning path.  Per Point reports show distance between tuning points and a list of information broken up into a point-by-point basis.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Reports:
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\i\fs20 \tab Region Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_region_summary.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\<region_name> folder and includes region-wide information on:
\par \tab \tab Number of objects
\par \tab \tab Number of enemies
\par \tab \tab Total possible experience from all objects
\par \tab \tab Total possible experience from all enemies
\par \tab \tab Total possible gold available
\par \tab \tab Total possible gold available from enemies
\par \tab \tab Total number of spells, potions, melee weapons, ranged weapons, armor, \tab \tab \tab shields, and their cumulative gold value
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li2160\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0 {\fs20 Total number of monster-owned spells, potions, melee weapons, ranged weapons, armor, shields, and their cumulative gold value. 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 \tab \tab Types of monsters and how many of each}{\i\fs20 
\par \tab 
\par \tab Path Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_ <tuning_path_name>_path_summary.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\<region_name> folder and includes
 the same information as the region summary; however, this report will generate the information for each tuning path in the region:
\par }{\i\fs20 \tab 
\par \tab All Item Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_ <tuning_path_name>_all_items.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\
<region_name> folder and contains the Template Name, Scid, Level, Class, Damage, Defense, Gold Value and Magical modifiers of all items along the path.
\par }{\i\fs20 
\par \tab Placed Item Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_ <tuning_path_name>_placed_items.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\
<region_name> folder and contains the Template Name, Scid, Level, Class, Damage, Defense, Gold Value and Magical modifiers of all placed items along the path.
\par }{\i\fs20 
\par \tab Enemy Item Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_ <tuning_path_name>_enemy_items.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\<region_name> folder and contains the Template Name, Scid, Level, Class, Damage, Defense, Gold Value a
nd Magical modifiers of all enemy owned items along the path.
\par }{\i\fs20 
\par \tab Container Item Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_ <tuning_path_name>_container_items.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\<region_name> folder and conta
ins the Template Name, Scid, Level, Class, Damage, Defense, Gold Value and Magical modifiers of container items along the path.
\par }{\i\fs20 
\par \tab Enemy Summary ~
\par \tab }{\fs20 This report, titled <region_name>_ <tuning_path_name>_enemies.txt, will appear in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\Tuning\\
<region_name> folder and contains the Template Name, Hit Points, Experience Value, Total Gold Value (including items), and Actual Gold carried for each monster on the tuning path, as well as the total number of enemies, the tota
l possible experience from enemies, the total enemy hit points, and the total gold available from the enemies.
\par }{\i\fs20 
