\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_PATH_BATCH_GENERATION}}}{\b\fs20\ul Batch Tuning Path Data Generation:
\par 
\par }{\fs20 This tool allows the user to generate any of the tuning reports for any selected region or combination of regions, as well as generating a master report and using tuning loads for reports.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Select Regions:
\par }{\fs20 By using the directory tree structure, the user can select which maps and regions for which reports will be generated.  The root map must be checked (selected) along with any regions selected within that map.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Use Tuning Loads:
\par }{\fs20 In many of the reports, numbers generated are based on POSSIBLE}{\i\fs20  }{\fs20 
values based on pcontent randomness.  By selecting the "Use Tuning Loads" option, the editor will assign actual items to monsters and containers so that specific values can be generated as opposed to maximum possible values.
\par 
\par NOTE ~ Do NOT save a region if tuning loads have been generated.  Saving the region after doing so would save all of the specific items rather than the pconten variables that generated them.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Generate Master Statistics:
\par }{\fs20 Selecting this option will generate a master report that will cover all of the selected regions.  The report will be named Master_Summary.txt and will be located in the \\My Documents\\Dungeon Siege\\Editor\\
Tuning folder.  It will show the total distance along the tuning path (in meters), the total number of enemies for the
 selected regions, the total experience available in the selected regions, and the total gold attainable (including item value) for selected regions.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Select All:
\par }{\fs20 Clicking on this button with any map or region selected will select all additional regions within the associated map.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Deselect All:
\par }{\fs20 Clicking on this button with any map or region selected will deselect all regions within the associated map.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Select Map:
\par }{\fs20 Clicking on this button will select the individual highlighted map or region.
\par }{\i\fs20\ul 
\par Deselect Map:
\par }{\fs20 Clicking on this button will deselect the individual highlighted map or region.
\par 
