\par }{\f1\fs20 \page }{\cs19\f1\fs20\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs19\super #}{ HIDD_DIALOG_DECAL}}}{\b\fs20\ul 
Decal Properties:
\par }{\fs20 
\par This tool is used to define settings for individual decals.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Settings:
\par }{\fs20 This area displays the ID number for the decal and has a checkbox for the user to select whether or not the decal is visible.  The visibility of the decal can later be altered by triggers.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Dimensions:
\par }{\fs20 This section allows the user to define the Horizontal and Vertical measurements of the decal.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Orientation:
\par }{\fs20 In this area, the user can set the orientation of the decal along its X, Y, and Z-axis.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Planes:
\par }{\fs20 By adjusting the Near and Far Plane settings, the user can define the look of a decal at its minimum and maximum view distances by setting the scalability.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Texture:
\par }{\fs20 This area displays the currently used texture address.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul LOD:
\par }{\fs20 Level of Detail \endash  Similar to LODFI, this number defines the amount of detail devoted to the decal.  The higher the number is, the greater the detail will be.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs20\ul Position:
\par }{\fs20 This area displays the current X,Y,Z-axis settings and the node on which the decal is situated.}{\i\fs20\ul 
\par 
\par Related Editor Dialogue Windows:
